nst retained mathematical inputs; no new Lean declaration, elaborated dependency, cross-model transport, Comparator acceptance or independent proof certification is asserted.","citation_ids":["authored_r8_scalar_finite_maximum_concentration"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_deductions_review_20261026"],"id":"scalar.finite_maximum_concentration","kind":"claim","label":"Concentration of the finite SK maximum","locator":"Long record §11.1.2, passage gibbs-comparison, Gaussian Lipschitz bound and concentration estimate","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For n>=2, M_n=max_sigma H_n(sigma)/n is sqrt((n-1)/(2n^2))-Lipschitz in the independent standard Gaussian SK couplings. Gaussian concentration gives Pr(|M_n-E M_n|>a)<=2 exp(-n^2 a^2/(n-1)); E M_n tends to P_star, hence M_n tends to P_star in probability. No effective mean-bias rate is supplied. The concentration bound is for every a>0.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_maximum_concentration","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_maximum_concentration","id":"field:f9df6715804c9cf0ad1106604092a47272e984a42f607839cefa593a3ebe6c7c","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_maximum_concentration","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/assumptions.qaoa_model_and_limits"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.sampled_finite_instance_optimum","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.sampled_finite_instance_optimum%22%2C%22scalar.finite_maximum_concentr